{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790676783,"nonce":"rjDsddj9AN1h+iYhSSXcWBT5qWU=","title":"Add a runtime Future carrier for asynchronous native APIs","message":"Ash has fibers and scheduler waiters, but no shared Haxe Future\u003cT\u003e object that a native library can complete after returning. This blocks generated bindings for APIs such as WebGPU: WebIDL Promise\u003cT\u003e operations need one stable language-level type, while wgpu completes requests and mapping operations from callbacks or worker tasks.\n\nAdd an Ash Future\u003cT\u003e surface and a C-shaped completion ABI suitable for native libraries and wasm side modules. The minimum surface should let Haxe await, inspect readiness, and attach a continuation, and let native code create a pending future then resolve or reject it exactly once. Awaiting a pending future should park the current Ash fiber through the runtime table rather than busy-wait or block the scheduler lane. Resolution from a foreign thread must safely retain the value or exception until the owning runtime resumes the waiter.\n\nThe xgpu binding generator will map WebIDL Promise\u003cT\u003e to this type. Caribou already exposes caribou.Future\u003cT\u003e; Rayzor exposes rayzor.concurrent.Future\u003cT\u003e, though its current lazy-closure construction will also need an adapter for externally completed operations. Ash should expose the same semantic contract without depending on either runtime's object layout.\n\nAcceptance:\n\n- Haxe can receive Future\u003cT\u003e from a native call and await the typed result.\n- Native and wasm side-module code can create, resolve, and reject a future through a stable C ABI.\n- completion is thread-safe, single-assignment, and wakes parked Ash fibers.\n- values and errors stay rooted until observed, including across collection.\n- native and wasm tests cover ready-before-await, await-before-ready, rejection, duplicate completion, and collection while pending.","files":null}]}